      "text": "Step 4: Now, we need to find the length of \\(AD\\) and \\(BD\\). We use the Pythagorean theorem in triangles \\(ACD\\) and \\(BCD\\):\n\\[ AD^2 + CD^2 = AC^2 \\]\n\\[ BD^2 + CD^2 = BC^2 \\]\nLet \\(AD = x\\) and \\(BD = 17 - x\\). Then:\n\\[ x^2 + \\left(\\frac{120}{17}\\right)^2 = 8^2 \\]\n\\[ (17 - x)^2 + \\left(\\frac{120}{17}\\right)^2 = 15^2 \\]",
